# Data Pipeline Rules

## Shape
- Numbered steps `01_*`…`08_*` scrape one source each into `data/raw/`. `10_canonical.ts` joins all seven off the ECI 543-PC spine into `data/canonical/mps.json` + `parties.json`.
- Run via `tsx`; no build step. Import siblings with explicit `.ts` extensions; import shared logic from `../lib/...` (and app-shared code from `../../lib/...`).
- Never move `data/` — steps read/write it via `new URL('../data/...', import.meta.url)`.

## Entity resolution
- Constituency-anchored: exact `state|constituency` match first, then constituency-only, then fuzzy `tokenSortRatio >= 90`. Name-confirm winners with `tokenSortRatio`.
- State normalisation + aliases live in `pipeline/lib/text.ts` (`normState`, `STATE_ALIASES`). Reuse them; never re-declare.

## Scoring
- All weights/caps and `calculateScore()` live in `lib/format/scoring.ts`, re-exported by `pipeline/lib/scoring.ts`. The pipeline imports them — no inline numbers in `10_canonical.ts`.
- After any scoring or join change, run `npm run canonical` and confirm the `data/canonical/mps.json` diff is intended (row count must stay 543; scores in [0,100]).

## Sourcing
- Every emitted field maps to a registry in `lib/sources.ts` and (if persisted) a `FACTMAP` entry in `lib/schema-constants.ts`.
- Handle missing data as `null`; never infer. Wrap fetch/parse in try/catch; rely on axios-retry for transient failures.
